# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  llm-wiki — runtime configuration
#
#  Copy to `.env` and edit:      cp .env.example .env
#  `.env` is gitignored; THIS file is committed and must never hold a real secret.
#
#  Read by docker-compose automatically. For a bare-metal run, export it first:
#      set -a; . ./.env; set +a; python3 -m wikikb serve
#  (every value below is also a plain CLI flag — the flag wins over the env var)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 0. OPERATION MODE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE application-level switch. Two modes, and they are ADDITIVE — `online` is a
# strict superset of `airgapped`, so a client written against one works verbatim
# against the other.
#
#   airgapped   (DEFAULT) Serves the vault + MCP, and the PDF write surface:
#               PUT /upload → the file is stored AND the conversion chain is
#               queued (pdf → corpus → immutable reference notes → crosslinked
#               Markdown). Opens no outbound connection, ever.
#   online      Everything above, PLUS the web-scraper surface (POST /scrape,
#               GET /scrape/sources). Not implemented yet — the endpoints are
#               mounted and answer 501; wikikb/scrape/scrape.py is the seam.
#
# In airgapped mode the scrape paths answer exactly like an unknown path and are
# absent from /openapi.json, so a sealed instance does not advertise a surface it
# refuses to serve. GET /health reports the live mode and its capabilities.
#
# A TYPO REFUSES TO START (exit 2) rather than falling back to a default — a mode
# is a security posture, and silently getting the wrong one is the failure that
# check exists to prevent. `offline` is accepted as an alias for `airgapped`.
WIKIKB_MODE=airgapped


# ── 1. WHERE THE CONTENT LIVES ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The HOST directory bind-mounted into the container. Everything the knowledge
# base needs lives under one parent, so migrating between machines is a copy of
# this single directory — page tiers, the immutable reference/_sources tiers,
# the generated indexes, taxonomy.md and .manifest.json all travel together.
#
# Seed it once from the repo:      cp -a ./vault/. /srv/llm-wiki/vault/
# Move it to another host:         copy that directory. That is the whole migration.
#
# Windows: use a forward-slash path, e.g. C:/Users/you/llm-wiki/vault
HOST_VAULT_DIR=./vault

# Host dir for state that is ABOUT the vault but rebuildable — the dense embedding
# index. Kept separate so it never bloats a vault copy; if you lose it, rebuild
# with `python3 -m wikikb embed`. Safe to delete.
HOST_STATE_DIR=./.wiki-state

# Where the vault is mounted INSIDE the container. Must match the compose mount.
# `paths.py` honours this; leaving it unset makes the code fall back to <repo>/vault,
# which is NOT what you want in a container.
WIKIKB_VAULT_ROOT=/data/vault

# Staging for an in-flight PDF/docs harvest (pdf_to_corpus -> corpus_to_vault).
# Points inside the mounted volume so a half-finished import survives a restart.
WIKIKB_CORPORA_DIR=/data/corpora


# ── 2. HTTP SURFACE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Port INSIDE the container. Change HOST_PORT (below) to move the published port
# without touching this.
WIKIKB_PORT=8642

# Host-side published port — what you actually browse to. Only compose reads this.
HOST_PORT=8642

# Bind address. 0.0.0.0 is correct INSIDE a container (loopback there is reachable
# only from inside it); `docker run -p` is what controls real exposure. Bare-metal
# default is 127.0.0.1 — do not widen it without setting WIKIKB_API_TOKEN.
WIKIKB_BIND=0.0.0.0

# Mount point for MCP-over-HTTP. Default /mcp; change only if it collides with a
# reverse-proxy route. A leading slash is optional (`api/mcp` is normalized to
# `/api/mcp`). Relocating it does not widen the surface — the old path then answers
# exactly like any unknown path.
WIKIKB_MCP_PATH=/mcp


# ── 3. AUTH ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# UNSET  = no auth (fine for loopback-only).
# SET    = `Authorization: Bearer <token>` required on every endpoint except
#          /health (left open because kubelet-style probes cannot send headers).
#          /openapi.json and /docs ARE gated — an API map is not probe traffic.
# REQUIRED whenever the service is reachable from a real interface.
#   generate:  openssl rand -hex 32
# WIKIKB_API_TOKEN=

# Comma-separated Origins allowed to POST to the MCP endpoint. Only enforced when
# a browser actually sends an Origin header — the DNS-rebinding guard. Backend
# callers (n8n, agents) send none and are unaffected.
# WIKIKB_MCP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-ui.example.com


# ── 4. INGEST (WRITE SURFACE — OFF BY DEFAULT) ───────────────────────────────
# 1/true/yes/on enables the write surface in BOTH modes:
#     PUT  /upload/<domain>/<file>.pdf   store a PDF (raw body, not multipart)
#     POST /ingest/<domain>              queue the conversion chain by hand
# Writes land ONLY in vault/_sources/<domain>/_raw/pdfs/, never the immutable
# reference tier. Disabled, both paths are indistinguishable from an unknown path.
# Leave unset unless you actually want a network-writable surface.
# WIKIKB_ALLOW_UPLOAD=1

# An upload TRIGGERS the conversion by default: pdf_to_corpus --append →
# corpus_to_vault → build (whose crosslink step is what links the new document to
# the other Markdown files). It runs as a BACKGROUND JOB on a single serialized
# worker — `build` regenerates whole-vault artifacts, so two at once would
# interleave writes — and the PUT returns a job_id to poll at GET /jobs/<id>.
#
# Set to 0 for store-only uploads, then batch several drops into one build with
# POST /ingest/<domain>. Note the chain lands the document as an immutable
# REFERENCE NOTE; synthesis pages are still authored against it (INGEST, CLAUDE.md).
# WIKIKB_AUTO_INGEST=0

# Per-step ceiling for a job, in seconds (default 1800). A full `build` on a large
# vault is minutes; this only exists so a wedged step cannot park the single worker
# forever and silently stall every job behind it.
# WIKIKB_JOB_TIMEOUT=1800


# ── 5. OPTIONAL LLM TIER (OFF BY DEFAULT) ────────────────────────────────────
# Absent these, `ask` returns EXTRACTIVE answers (quoted source spans). Setting
# them enables synthesized prose through the local gateway. The gate, citations
# and banners apply either way.
#   WIKI_LLM=local
#   WIKI_LLM_MODEL=ollama/qwen2.5:3b
# From inside a container, host.docker.internal reaches an Ollama on the host.
#   WIKI_LLM_API_BASE=http://host.docker.internal:11434
# Known trap (CLAUDE.md): a stale api_base makes the gateway silently return None
# and every answer quietly falls back to extractive. If prose vanishes, check this first.
